.Dd October 5, 2026
.Dt SP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm sp
.Nd use encrypted item vaults and device-local hardware credentials
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The app, AutoFill and CLI share an encrypted device-local Core Data store.
Independent item changes commit locally before CKSyncEngine delivery.
Device agreement and signing keys are generated in Secure Enclave.
Same-account private vaults connect automatically while an existing device is unlocked.
.Sh COMMANDS
Use command --help for complete arguments.
Secret commands include read, write, list, delete, run, inject and item.
Values are supplied by hidden prompt or stdin.
References use sp://vault/item/[section/]field.
Rename changes references that use names.
.Pp
Vault init creates a vault; vault list discovers vaults; vault sync requests delivery.
Vault backup exports local transferable contents to a portable archive and a
separate generated key file. It cannot certify complete remote inventory.
Vault restore-backup requires both files and a fresh --restore-id UUID retained
for retries. Use --dry-run to validate before creating an independent owned vault.
Hardware private keys and membership are not restored. Only archive v2 is accepted;
v1 archives are unsupported. Derived health results and credential registrations
are excluded.
.Pp
Device removal and permanent cloud-vault deletion are preview features awaiting
physical-device acceptance. Vault deletion is enabled in Development; Production
requires MOP_VAULT_DELETION and the separate V3 Production review gate.
Cross-account sharing, general document import and credential-account management
are unimplemented. Account recovery is implemented with physical acceptance pending.
Secret references accept only sp://; retired mop:// values are rejected.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Fl -vault Ar NAME-OR-UUID
constrains selection. Management requires selection when multiple vaults exist.
.Pp
.Fl -offline
prevents network use. Local reads and item saves remain available.
Offline clients cannot detect unobserved remote changes or prove freshness.
.Pp
.Fl -local-save
returns after durable local commit. Otherwise CLI writes normally wait up to
20 seconds for exact delivery receipts. A timeout reports pending receipt IDs
and exits nonzero while preserving queued work. Do not repeat the write.
.Pp
Cloud vaults require the shared App Group store; isolated --state-directory
storage is not supported for them.
.Sh SECURITY
Operational access requires signed provisioning, matching Keychain/App Group
and CloudKit configuration, supported hardware and authentication.
GUI authorization lasts until lock/expiry; CLI commands own their sessions;
AutoFill authenticates afresh. Plaintext and temporary item keys enter process memory.
.Pp
Read and inject release plaintext to stdout or files. Run passes plaintext
in the child environment. That child, dependencies and descendants are trusted
with the secrets. Exact-byte output masking does not constrain transformed
output, files, diagnostics or network traffic.
.Pp
Same-account admission explicitly trusts the authenticated private iCloud container.
An attacker able to write through that channel may obtain admission while an
existing unlocked device processes the request. Existing trust pins cannot be
replaced by discovery. Signed per-item revisions do not prove global inventory
completeness or freshness.
.Pp
Keep portable archives and their keys separately. Device-local keys cannot be
exported or restored. 2ndPass is not independently audited.
.Sh SEE ALSO
The project README, docs/VAULT.md, docs/SECURITY.md, docs/BACKUPS.md and
docs/VALIDATION.md describe current behavior and remaining acceptance checks.
.Sh SUBSCRIPTION STATUS
.Nm subscription status
.Op Fl Fl json
.Op Fl Fl offline
.Pp
Report shared Pro subscription evidence without restricting commands.
Operational commands emit a concise status on stderr; stdout and exit codes
retain their existing meanings. Offline checks use previously verified evidence
through its expiration or billing-grace deadline, without an extension.
Development CloudKit builds are explicitly exempt.
